Project Overview

This project is designed to manage and catalog automotive parts, specifically focusing on BMW OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) parts and upgrades. 
The database schema supports tracking of various parts, their categories, brands, pricing, compatibility, and vendor details. 
It also includes an audit trail to record changes made to the database for traceability and transparency.

The project utilizes an ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipeline to manage and transform data from multiple sources, ensuring a comprehensive catalog that can be used for various purposes.

This is a source that I can access and search like an end-user for parts for my personal BMW E34 car.

The goal is to streamline the management of parts and pricing data, providing an efficient and scalable solution for part identification, upgrades, and replacements.

Database Schema for Parts Catalog ETL Project
This schema defines the structure of the parts catalog database used for the ETL project. The database contains tables for storing brands, categories, parts, prices, vendors, compatibility details, and change history.

Data sources:
www.realoem.com - BMW OEM parts catalog
www.ecstuning.com - BMW aftermarket parts and upgrades
www.bmwpartsdirect.com - BMW OEM parts and accessories
www.bimmerworld.com - BMW performance parts and accessories
www.fcpeuro.com - European car parts and accessories

Tables
brands
Stores information about the brands of parts.

brand_id: UUID (Primary Key)
brand_name: VARCHAR (Unique)
categories
Stores information about part categories.

category_id: UUID (Primary Key)
category_name: VARCHAR (Unique)
change_history
Tracks changes to the database schema, tables, and data.

log_id: UUID (Primary Key)
schema_name: TEXT
table_name: TEXT
operation: TEXT (Insert/Update/Delete)
changed_by: TEXT
change_time: TIMESTAMP
old_data: JSONB
new_data: JSONB
compatibility
Stores information about part compatibility (model, engine code, and years).

compatibility_id: UUID (Primary Key)
model: VARCHAR
engine_code: VARCHAR
years: VARCHAR
parts
Stores detailed information about parts.

part_id: UUID (Primary Key)
part_number: VARCHAR (Unique)
name: VARCHAR
description: TEXT
category_id: UUID (Foreign Key referencing categories)
brand_id: UUID (Foreign Key referencing brands)
compatibility_id: UUID (Foreign Key referencing compatibility)
prices
Stores price details for parts.

price_id: UUID (Primary Key)
part_id: UUID (Foreign Key referencing parts)
vendor_id: UUID (Foreign Key referencing vendors)
price_zar: NUMERIC
price_date: TIMESTAMP
vendors
Stores vendor information.

vendor_id: UUID (Primary Key)
vendor_name: VARCHAR
website: TEXT
Relationships
parts.category_id references categories.category_id
parts.brand_id references brands.brand_id
parts.compatibility_id references compatibility.compatibility_id
prices.part_id references parts.part_id
prices.vendor_id references vendors.vendor_id
